---
interface Props {
  releases: number;
  dated: number;
  medianAvailabilityLagH: number | null;
  /** Launches whose market held 0.9 before the announcement, and how many of those had a public precursor. */
  early90: number;
  early90Prompted: number;
  /** Skill of the raw market forecast against the base rate at 72h. */
  marketSkill72: number;
}
const { releases, dated, medianAvailabilityLagH, early90, early90Prompted, marketSkill72 } = Astro.props;
const lag = medianAvailabilityLagH === null ? 'about the same time as' : `${Math.round(Math.abs(medianAvailabilityLagH) * 60)} minutes ${medianAvailabilityLagH < 0 ? 'before' : 'after'}`;
---
<aside class="limits panel" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
  <h2 id="limits-title" class="tiny glow-y">WHAT THIS CAN'T DO</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>It mostly detects launches after they happen.</strong> The median model reached OpenRouter {lag} its announcement. Registry listings, feeds and HN confirm a launch; they rarely precede it.</li>
    <li><strong>DROPCON is an activity index, not a probability.</strong> Recent launches raise it. Its market input, read on its own, {marketSkill72 < 0 ? 'scores worse than' : 'barely beats'} always guessing the base rate (<a href="#calibration">Brier table</a>). This page scores that input, not the DROPCON level itself.</li>
    <li><strong>The markets aggregate leaks rather than foresee launches.</strong> Of {early90} launches whose market reached 0.9 before the announcement, {early90Prompted} followed a public leak, a press report or the lab's own notice (<a href="#splits">splits</a>).</li>
    <li><strong>n is small.</strong> {releases} launches, {dated} of them with a market that dates the day. One lab changing its habits moves every number here.</li>
    <li><strong>The dashboard's own history starts 2026-09-23.</strong> No launch before then can be replayed through the live score, and HN point counts cannot be replayed at all: Algolia only returns final totals.</li>
  </ul>
</aside>
<style>
  .limits { border-color: rgba(255, 226, 28, 0.45); }
  .limits h2 { font-size: var(--fs-head); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .limits ul { display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .limits li { padding-left: 18px; position: relative; font-size: 19px; }
  .limits li::before { content: '\25B8'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--yellow); }
  .limits strong { color: #fff; font-weight: 400; }
</style>
